    "details": "<p><strong data-start=\"241\" data-end=\"258\"> PARALLAX 2026 &ndash; Reality, Reimagined</strong></p>\n<p><strong data-start=\"241\" data-end=\"258\">PARALLAX 2026</strong> is an inter-college hackathon focused on <strong data-start=\"300\" data-end=\"375\">Augmented Reality (AR), Virtual Reality (VR), and Extended Reality (XR)</strong>. The hackathon challenges students to think beyond conventional applications and build innovative, immersive solutions to real-world problems.</p>\n<p>Participants will explore the potential of immersive technologies to transform <strong data-start=\"599\" data-end=\"697\">education, healthcare, tourism, gaming, industry, entertainment, and other real-world domains.</strong></p>\n<p>Theme: <strong data-start=\"714\" data-end=\"738\">Reality, Reimagined.</strong></p>\n<p>The goal is to create solutions that demonstrate how AR/VR/XR can solve problems, enhance experiences, and create meaningful real-world impact.</p>\n<p><strong>Hackathon Structure</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 &ndash; Online Assessment</strong></p>\n<p>The first round will be conducted <strong data-start=\"978\" data-end=\"988\">online</strong> and will consist of a technical assessment designed to evaluate participants' knowledge of:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1082\" data-end=\"1258\">\n<li data-section-id=\"ebk2sh\" data-start=\"1082\" data-end=\"1105\">AR/VR/XR fundamentals</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"zmloda\" data-start=\"1106\" data-end=\"1129\">Unity &amp; Unreal Engine</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"11kbltu\" data-start=\"1130\" data-end=\"1157\">3D graphics and modelling</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1pvcswb\" data-start=\"1158\" data-end=\"1175\">Computer vision</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"147kytx\" data-start=\"1176\" data-end=\"1194\">Game development</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"139g3en\" data-start=\"1195\" data-end=\"1219\">Immersive technologies</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1fmcdu8\" data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1258\">Problem-solving and logical thinking</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Participants/teams qualifying this round will advance to the next rounds.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &ndash; Ideation and PPT Submission</strong></p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams will participate in this round.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Teams will develop an AR/VR/XR-based solution around the given problem statement(s) and present a <strong>working prototype with demonstration video and PPT submission.</strong></p>\n<p>Participants will be evaluated on:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1610\" data-end=\"1732\">\n<li data-section-id=\"zno41x\" data-start=\"1610\" data-end=\"1622\">Innovation</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1b8ahu1\" data-start=\"1623\" data-end=\"1649\">Technical implementation</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1drlr1b\" data-start=\"1650\" data-end=\"1667\">Use of AR/VR/XR</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1ln14ta\" data-start=\"1668\" data-end=\"1694\">Problem-solving approach</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"m9uzpb\" data-start=\"1695\" data-end=\"1714\">Real-world impact</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"16po99j\" data-start=\"1715\" data-end=\"1732\">User experience</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 3 &ndash; Grand Finale</strong></p>\n<p>The top-performing teams from Round 2 will qualify for the <strong data-start=\"1820\" data-end=\"1836\">Grand Finale</strong>.</p>\n<p>Finalists will present their solution and demonstrate their working model before a panel of judges.</p>\n<p><strong>This round will also be online.</strong></p>\n<p>The final evaluation will consider:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1980\" data-end=\"2117\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1con39a\" data-start=\"1980\" data-end=\"2006\">Innovation &amp; originality</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1t8bgpr\" data-start=\"2007\" data-end=\"2029\">Technical complexity</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"mxx23r\" data-start=\"2030\" data-end=\"2055\">AR/VR/XR implementation</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"6d86l5\" data-start=\"2056\" data-end=\"2074\">Practical impact</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1yc90gn\" data-start=\"2075\" data-end=\"2088\">Scalability</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"17bzguu\" data-start=\"2089\" data-end=\"2096\">UI/UX</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"xnv84u\" data-start=\"2097\" data-end=\"2117\">Presentation &amp; Q&amp;A</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2138\" data-end=\"2433\">\n<li data-section-id=\"10bte9m\" data-start=\"2138\" data-end=\"2187\">Open to <strong data-start=\"2148\" data-end=\"2168\">college students</strong> from across India.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1khqqng\" data-start=\"2188\" data-end=\"2269\">Students from any engineering/technology or related discipline can participate.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1rzztzk\" data-start=\"2270\" data-end=\"2322\">Participation will be in teams of <strong>1</strong><strong data-start=\"2306\" data-end=\"2321\">&ndash;4 members</strong>.(<strong>Either individual)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Participants must carry a valid college ID during the offline rounds.</p>\n<p>Who Should Participate?</p>\n<p>&nbsp;PARALLAX 2026 is for students interested in:</p>\n<p><strong data-start=\"3111\" data-end=\"3241\">AR &bull; VR &bull; XR &bull; Unity &bull; Unreal Engine &bull; 3D Development &bull; Game Development &bull; Computer Vision &bull; Immersive Technology &bull; Innovation</strong></p>\n<p><strong data-start=\"3245\" data-end=\"3293\">Step beyond the screen. Build a new reality.</strong></p>",
    "end_date": "2026-10-05T12:00:00+05:30",
